#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084294} :activity/id #uuid "50780a4d-0efe-5dba-905f-c67e5889db4b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050957 :topic/id #uuid "755ddd1f-5d88-5a57-8c26-e4a1505b3fff" :topic/math-academy-id 749} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084294 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084492 :tutorial/content "When the $n$th term $a_n$ of an infinite series involves $n$th powers, we can determine whether the series converges or diverges using the **root test**.\n\nSuppose we have a series\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{n =1} ^\\infty a_n\n$$\n\nsuch that\n\n$$\na_n \\geq 0\n$$\n\nfor all\n\n$$\nn \\geq 1\n$$\n\n. We define $L$ as the following limit:\n\n$$\nL = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\sqrt [n] {a_n} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\left({a_n}\\right)^{1/n}\n$$\n\nThen, the root test states the following:\n\n- if $L < 1$, the series converges.\n- if $L >1$ or $L = \\infty$, the series diverges.\n- if $L = 1$, the root test is inconclusive.\n\nLet's use the root test to show that the following geometric series converges:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac {1} {2^n}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our sequence $a_n$ is defined as\n\n$$\na_n = \\dfrac{1}{2^n}, \\qquad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nTo apply the root test, we calculate the limit of $\\sqrt[n]{a_n}$ as $n\\to\\infty{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL &= lim_(n → ∞)\\sqrt[n]{\\frac{1}{2^{n}}} \\\\\n&= lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{\\sqrt[n]{1}}{\\sqrt[n]{2^{n}}} \\\\\n&= lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nL=\\dfrac12 < 1\n$$\n\nour series converges by the root test.\n\nFinally, when applying the root test, it's worth bearing the following limit facts in mind:\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sqrt [n] {a} = 1$ for $a > 0$\n- $\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sqrt [n] {n} = 1$\n- $\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\sqrt [n] {\\dfrac 1 {n!}} = 0$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3a3259b2-b4b5-580c-a5f2-d1718c65a022" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6116 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6c859a87-7f6f-521b-9bcf-5d8691ae2dbc" :step/math-academy-id 37147 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084295}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084295 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083340 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083143 :question/id #uuid "c0a47f18-97ca-5bbe-8825-f088318a4cb4" :question/math-academy-id "e-9875"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "469975d9-f2a2-5e3e-9f26-cee3557cb88a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049983} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050706}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083527} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083823}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Root Test to a Convergent Series"} :step/id #uuid "9c652735-cd8b-57c0-9f3a-55d6a813833a" :step/math-academy-id 37149 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084296}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084296 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083341 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083144 :question/id #uuid "031d607b-0478-5676-ac4b-596431ca9481" :question/math-academy-id "e-9876"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cab29074-3281-5c02-9a2b-423077675aef" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083539} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233443}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Root Test in Divergent and Inconclusive Cases"} :step/id #uuid "b30928b4-83ea-54cf-be19-db7f024517fb" :step/math-academy-id 37150}] :activity/title "The Root Test" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186083440}]}
